---
description: Project-specific import restrictions for TS/TSX. These are enforced by ESLint at error level, and `yarn test:code` runs with --max-warnings=0, so violations fail CI.
globs: ["packages/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "excalidraw-app/**/*.{ts,tsx}"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Imports

- Import cross-package code via aliases, not long relative paths:
  `@excalidraw/common`, `@excalidraw/element`, `@excalidraw/math`, `@excalidraw/utils`, `@excalidraw/excalidraw`.
- Inside `packages/excalidraw/`, never import from a barrel / `index` file (`.`, `..`, `@excalidraw/excalidraw`).
  Import the specific module directly instead.
- Never import `jotai` directly. Use `editor-jotai` (library code) or `app-jotai` (app code).
- Use separate type imports: `import type { Foo } from "..."` rather than mixing types into a value import.

```ts
// BAD
import { someUtil } from "../../../common/src/utils";
import { atom } from "jotai";
import { AppState, getDefaultAppState } from "@excalidraw/excalidraw";

// GOOD
import { someUtil } from "@excalidraw/common";
import { atom } from "../editor-jotai";
import { getDefaultAppState } from "../appState";
import type { AppState } from "../types";
```
